### Auditor-Defense Compliance Framing (PCI DSS v4.0.1 & CISA BOD 26-04)

- **PCI DSS v4.0.1 (Requirements 6.3.1 & 11.3.1):** Risk-based prioritization combines authoritative CVSS provenance (`NVD > CNA > GHSA > OSV > Scanner-Supplied`), CISA KEV active exploitation status, FIRST EPSS v5 exploit prediction probabilities/percentiles, and asset exposure context. Documented deferrals carry explicit owners, compensating/environmental assumptions, and expiration dates, with automated stale-assumption re-evaluation on every scan.
- **CISA BOD 26-04 / SSVC:** Remediation SLAs (`3-day + Forensic Triage`, `14-day`, `60-day`, `Fix on Upgrade`) follow Stakeholder-Specific Vulnerability Categorization (SSVC) decision trees over public exposure, exploitation maturity, automatability, and technical impact rather than raw scanner severity labels alone.

